    '',
    'The rendering: draw the buffer as a polyline on canvas — each new data point shifts the entire chart LEFT by one pixel (a rolling window); use ctx.drawImage(canvas, -1, 0) to shift the existing chart left, then draw the new point at the right edge — the FASTEST update (one drawImage + one line).',
    '',
    'The decimation: when the data arrives faster than the display rate (100Hz data on a 60fps display) — DOWNSAMPLE: keep every Nth point, or min/max/avg per bucket (the MinMaxDecimation preserves the peaks and valleys — critical for waveform displays).',
